CATEGORIES -- what is here, grouped by what it is for=====================================================DOC/INDEX lists every program alphabetically and says what each one is.This is the same set in the order you want when you do not yet know thename: 1002 programs, of which 653 need nothing but this disk.  A star meansthe program wants Microware's cio -- see DOC/README-CIO.----------------------------------------------------------------------SHELLS (24)----------------------------------------------------------------------  Unix shells to sit beside OS-9's own -- bash and ksh bring history,  job control, and scripts that come across unchanged.  Shell helpers:   *checkenv         compares an environment variable with a value for a...      `checkenv <name> , <value>' with spaces round the comma.      Meant to return an error when they differ; it returns 0      either way.   *exist            test whether a file exists and answer in the exit...   *getenv           print or test an environment variable.  German...    hist             a command-line editor with history, in front of the...      A command-line editor with history in front of the shell. On      this console it prints a row of asterisks and returns at once.    if               conditional execution for a shell script: `if def...      bash's own `if' is a reserved word; `command if' reaches the      one on this disk.   *printenv         print the environment    printf           formatted print from the shell, as on Unix: widths...      printf as on Unix: `printf "%-8s|%5d\n" name 12'. Widths,      numbers and floating point all work.   *qp               expands back-quotes in a command line, which...      Runs its expanded command through Microware's `shell'.    run              runs a program with its input and output on the...      `run '<program> <args>'' with PORT naming a terminal: the      program runs with its input and output on that terminal.   *submit          